.claude/reference/env-vars.md:45:| `SESSION_COOKIE_SECRET` | Server-only HMAC-SHA256 signing secret, **≥ 32 bytes** (`openssl rand -hex 32`). Single authoritative reader: `getSessionCookieSecret()` (`src/lib/shared/session-cookie-secret.ts`), which throws when unset or short. Needed on **both** surfaces — Vercel and the Railway worker. Four consumers today: the approval session cookie (`src/lib/approval/cookies.ts`), the Zernio connect session cookie (`src/lib/zernio/connect-session-cookie.ts`), the account-offboarding keep-my-data token + fresh-auth stamp (`src/lib/account-offboarding/{tokens,destructive-auth}.ts`), and **(#644)** the Unsubscribe token admission gate + success receipt (`src/lib/solicitation/unsubscribe.ts`). **⚠️ Rotate ONLY via `SESSION_COOKIE_SECRET_PREVIOUS` (next row) — never by swapping this value alone.** The rollover procedure: set `SESSION_COOKIE_SECRET_PREVIOUS` to the **outgoing** value **and** `SESSION_COOKIE_SECRET` to the **new** one **in the same deploy**, on **both** surfaces; keep the previous key set for at least the statutory token lifetime (**≥ 30 days**) before clearing it. Two blast radii: **(1) statutory** — #644's admission gate keys on this secret while `token_hash` stays an *unkeyed* SHA-256, so a rotation does not corrupt the lookup, it makes every **already-delivered** unsubscribe link fail the gate. The token row stays perfectly valid and redeemable but is unreachable, the recipient gets 503 / the neutral page, and by §5.4's enumeration rule that is indistinguishable from a genuine unknown token — while CAN-SPAM §7704(a)(3) requires the link operate **≥ 30 days**. Current-plus-previous verification (#644) is what makes that survivable; **it covers the unsubscribe token + receipt ONLY.** **(2)** every outstanding keep-my-data offboarding link, which is a deterministic HMAC under this secret with only its hash persisted — that domain has **no** previous-key fallback yet, so a rotation still invalidates every outstanding keep-my-data link. Approval and Zernio connect cookies are short-lived and simply re-issue. **Worker boot asserts it on deployed lanes since #644** — `assertUnsubscribeTokenSecretConfigured()` (`src/lib/solicitation/unsubscribe.ts`, called from `worker/index.ts`) fails the boot outright, skipping local and `MOCK_EXTERNAL_APIS=true` runs, matching `assertAlertSinkEnv`. **This is deliberate and it will crash-loop a deployed worker that lacks the var** — that is the point: before #644 the only boot check was `assertAccountOffboardingEnv()`, gated on `ACCOUNT_OFFBOARDING_ENABLED` (documented Off below), so a worker missing this secret booted clean and then failed **every** well-formed unsubscribe with a 503 indistinguishable from a genuine unknown token. A crash-loop is a visible failure; that was a silent statutory one. ⚠️ **Deployment precondition, split by lane — owner decision at #644's merge, deviations D13.** **Railway staging:** set; confirmed before #644 shipped. **Railway prod:** deliberately **NOT** set, and #644 merged anyway — the prod `repworth-worker` is `Offline — never successfully deployed` (`deployment-guide.md` cloud-state table), so the gate has nothing to crash-loop. `RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT_NAME=production` is set on that environment, so `requiresProductionConfig()` returns true there the moment it boots **even though `NODE_ENV` is unset**: setting this var is a precondition of **the prod worker's first successful deploy** — scheduled with the Solicitation agent's go-live — not of any merge. **Vercel:** NOT boot-asserted (no boot phase) and fails **per-request** instead — see the landing-page note in #644's deviations D4 — so it must be set on Vercel prod before `/u/<token>` serves traffic. No `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` companion (invariant #13). |
.claude/reference/env-vars.md:46:| `SESSION_COOKIE_SECRET_PREVIOUS` | **Optional; empty in the steady state.** The OUTGOING `SESSION_COOKIE_SECRET` during a rollover, **≥ 32 bytes** under the same validation (a set-but-short value throws, and the worker boot gate `assertUnsubscribeTokenSecretConfigured()` crash-loops on it rather than letting a rollover typo surface as a 503 per opt-out). **Verification only — nothing is ever minted under it.** Read by `src/lib/solicitation/unsubscribe.ts`, which verifies the Unsubscribe token gate and the success receipt against the current key first and this one only on a miss. Server lane only (`src/lib/config/server.ts`), like `SESSION_COOKIE_SECRET` itself — both surfaces read it through `getServerConfig()`, so there is deliberately no worker-lane declaration. **Rollover:** set this to the outgoing value **and** `SESSION_COOKIE_SECRET` to the new one **in the same deploy** on Vercel + Railway; leave it set for **≥ 30 days** (CAN-SPAM §7704(a)(3)'s link-operating window), then clear it — clearing is what actually retires the old key. Scope note: this covers the #644 unsubscribe token + receipt only, **not** the account-offboarding keep-my-data token. Never logged. No `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` companion (invariant #13). |
.claude/reference/env-vars.md:646:| `ACCOUNT_OFFBOARDING_ENABLED` | Off | Server-only kill switch for owner offboarding. Leave off until the full 7-PR sequence lands and the staging dry-run passes. `true` is the only enabling value; worker startup rejects non-`true`/`false` configured values. No `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` companion. Browser surfaces learn offboarding state through authenticated server responses only. |
.claude/reference/env-vars.md:648:| `ACCOUNT_OFFBOARDING_PURGE_WINDOW_OVERRIDE_MS` | unset | **Staging / non-prod only.** Server-only shortener for the 30-day `delete_data` purge window so the staging dry-run does not block on the real wait. `getAccountOffboardingPurgeWindowOverrideMs()` returns `null` (refuses the override) when `NODE_ENV=production` **or** `VERCEL_ENV=production`, so it can never shorten the purge window in production. Never exposed to browser code; intentionally absent from `.env.example` so it is not mistaken for a normal var. Sibling poller tuning vars `ACCOUNT_OFFBOARDING_PURGE_INTERVAL_MS` (default 60000) and `ACCOUNT_OFFBOARDING_PURGE_BATCH_SIZE` (default 25, capped 100) are optional and safe in any env. The T-3d purge-reminder poller has the same optional tuning pair: `ACCOUNT_OFFBOARDING_PURGE_REMINDER_INTERVAL_MS` (default 60000) and `ACCOUNT_OFFBOARDING_PURGE_REMINDER_BATCH_SIZE` (default 25, capped 100). |
.claude/reference/env-vars.md:658:| `TRIAL_ENABLED` | **Off** | Card-up-front, Stripe-native 30-day free trial (migration 069). Server-authoritative; **no `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` companion** (inv #13). When `true` AND the account is a self-serve `pending_payment` account (eligibility per the trial spec §0.2 — decided in ONE place, `isTrialEligible` in `src/lib/payments/plan-activation.ts`, which also ANDs `SELF_SERVE_SIGNUP_ENABLED`; the two entry points spelled it separately and disagreed until PF-H2), both self-serve checkout entry points (`/api/billing/checkout`, `/api/onboarding/select-plan`) pass `trial: true` to `createCheckoutSession`, which adds `subscription_data.trial_period_days = TRIAL_PERIOD_DAYS`. Stripe charges **$0 now** and the resulting subscription comes back `status='trialing'`, which `checkout.session.completed` projects to the new explicit `'trialing'` account status via the single applier (`worker/ingress/stripe/apply-subscription-state.ts`). `'trialing'` is treated like `'active'` for entitlement everywhere EXCEPT recurring paid ranking tracking (SerpAPI) which stays active-only. Conversion `trialing→active` fires from `customer.subscription.updated` (status='active') only — the $0 trial-start invoice does NOT convert. Cancel-during-trial runs through existing offboarding `cancel_at_period_end`. The landing hero CTA — and, since the 2026-08-16 marketing truth pass, the `/how-it-works` and `/features` CTAs — become "Start your N-day free trial" only when this AND `SELF_SERVE_SIGNUP_ENABLED` are on. Reconcile poller has scoped corrective authority for stuck trialing rows. Worker startup does not hard-require it (default-off, additive). |
