docs/analytics/events.md:133:### `offboarding_started`
docs/analytics/events.md:135:- **Description:** Owner confirmed an account offboarding request.
docs/analytics/events.md:136:- **Owner:** account offboarding confirm transaction
docs/analytics/events.md:137:- **Source:** server-side, in the offboarding creation transaction (durable; not client-postable)
docs/analytics/events.md:139:- **Event key:** `offboarding_started:<offboarding_id>`
docs/analytics/events.md:144:### `offboarding_reactivated`
docs/analytics/events.md:146:- **Description:** Owner reactivated a cancel-only offboarding before teardown began.
docs/analytics/events.md:147:- **Owner:** account offboarding reactivation transaction
docs/analytics/events.md:150:- **Event key:** `offboarding_reactivated:<offboarding_id>`
docs/analytics/events.md:155:### `offboarding_teardown_completed`
docs/analytics/events.md:157:- **Description:** Worker finished all offboarding teardown steps.
docs/analytics/events.md:158:- **Owner:** Railway account offboarding teardown worker
docs/analytics/events.md:161:- **Event key:** `offboarding_teardown_completed:<offboarding_id>`
docs/analytics/events.md:162:- **Required properties:** `mode`, `status` (`churned` or `purge_scheduled`)
docs/analytics/events.md:166:### `offboarding_purged`
docs/analytics/events.md:168:- **Description:** Worker completed delete-data purge and retained only the lifecycle receipt.
docs/analytics/events.md:169:- **Owner:** Railway account offboarding purge worker
docs/analytics/events.md:170:- **Source:** worker-side, in the purge finalization transaction (durable; not client-postable)
docs/analytics/events.md:171:- **Distinct ID:** SHA-256 pseudonymous offboarding key
docs/analytics/events.md:172:- **Event key:** `offboarding_purged:<sha256(offboarding_id)>`
docs/analytics/events.md:175:- **Privacy notes:** no account, user, business, provider, or raw offboarding identifier is retained.
docs/analytics/events.md:259:- **Distinct ID:** account ID **when one is known**, else the suppression row id (`input.accountId ?? row.id`). The `accountId: null` path is not an accident — §5.2 post-purge redemption and unresolvable webhook sources both mint global rows with no account — and `analytics_events.distinct_id` is NOT NULL, so it needs *some* value. The consequence: an accountless global suppression mints a one-off PostHog person per row. **#644 shipped the first caller that actually reaches this path** — a token whose account was purged (§5.2) redeems with `account_id = NULL` — so the fallback is live, not hypothetical. Still acceptable at today's volume (nothing mints tokens until #630), but **#645/#627 should pick a stable sentinel** if accountless volume turns out to be non-trivial.
docs/analytics/events.md:272:- **Event key:** `solicitation_suppressed_at_dispatch_<ask_id>` — one refusal per Ask.
docs/analytics/events.md:312:- **Description:** One successful **QR redirect** (CONTEXT.md): a customer scanned a location's **Review QR** and was 302-redirected to that location's Google write-review page. Counted AFTER the resolve gates pass (existence, not archived, `subscriptionAllowsQrRedirect`, canonical place id) and never on a refusal — an unavailable-page serve emits nothing (it is a log line, not a metric). v1 counts every successful resolve, HEAD requests and prefetchers included (accepted noise, intake edge case). The name is registered in the `analytics_events.event_name` CHECK by **migration 115** — the DB CHECK, not the TS allowlist, is what admits the name.
