.claude/reference/arch-review-log.md:1396:| 2026-07-27 | 5 merges ≥ 5 threshold (#570, #571, #574, #575 — map-#528 completion wave; #583) + the #585/#586/#588/#589 debt sweep | map-#528 wave (run-engine executor, rival picker, Requests watch-mode, competitor delta digest), the debt sweep's four closures, and the CI/measurement surface (`ci:*` audits, fallow gate, `.claude/reference/*` allowlists) | 4 new findings, no blockers. **Carried-forward closures all confirmed.** R1 closed by #586 — `railway-replicas` rule at `scripts/ci/static-policy-audit.ts:790` + `worker/config/replica-identity.ts` wired from `worker/index.ts`/`worker/sentry.ts`; *detection without enforcement is the right posture* — Railway injects a per-replica id but no replica count, so no process can assert it is alone, and the one mechanically blockable path (config-as-code) IS blocked. #587 correctly scopes the residue. R2 closed by #588 — *verdict holds*: 15 typed helpers vs 29 files writing raw `INSERT INTO job_outbox`, and `src/lib/shared/job-outbox-status.ts` documents why a fragment seam would have been actively wrong (a bind parameter inside `ON CONFLICT … WHERE` defeats partial-index inference), so guarding the vocabulary is the correct seam. S1/S2 closed by #565 (`acquireCsvIngestLock` exported at `ingest.ts:380`; single terminal writer at `ingest.ts:394`). S3 shipped as built *with an answer* — `worker/jobs/solicitation-batch/failed-hook.ts` records an exhausted build on the run spine via `failSolicitationBatchRun`, so it is not "nowhere recorded"; not re-raised. **New: #590** (HIGH) `ci:live-db-suites` (`package.json:39`) is wired into neither `.github/workflows/ci.yml` nor `lefthook.yml` — the only one of 15 — while CLAUDE.md and #585's commit body both claim CI enforcement; the general defect is that the `ci:*` set is hand-spelled in three places with nothing forcing agreement, and `scripts/verify-gate.sh:60` already derives it correctly in the one place that does. This is the mechanism