.claude/reference/arch-review-log.md:1399:| 2026-08-18 | 8 counted merges ≥ 5 threshold — **measured as 11 by the counter's own rule**, across a 32-commit window (the solicitation send lane #657/#651/#652/#629/#858/#859/#860/#865/#872 + #665/#662; the uncounted three-tier design system #843–#846; the uncounted CI/tooling surface #847–#850/#854/#867) | Pathfinder pass, **windowed** (owner's call): 9 features charted — F1 approval lane, F2 Requests surface, F3 admin console, F4 email lane, F5 unsubscribe, F6 design system, F7 marketing, F8 CI enforcement, F9 purge verifier. Two extra axes: guard-integrity (42 mutations) and process. Artifacts `docs/reviews/PATHFINDER-2026-08-18/00-06` | **Headline: the code held its shape a FOURTH time — health 77 B → 77 B, maintainability 92.2 → 92.2, duplication 1.1% → 1.1%, 0 churn hotspots, high-complexity functions 153 → 122 — and three of this pass's own findings would have been WRONG if reasoned instead of measured.** (1) **F8 refuted the fix the pass was about to prescribe**: adding the four missing tables to `TENANT_TABLES` produces **63 red lines and 0 security fixes** (measured by copying the audit and running `--no-allowlist`); the real gap is the **bridge vocabulary** — `localScopedBindings:942` knows 3 shapes, `users` needs a 4th (`accounts.owner_user_id = users.id`, inbound FK on the parent) and a 5th. H5 is therefore three ORDERED steps. (2) **F3's boundary was wrong**: the import closure of its two halves intersects in **zero domain modules**, and the trust models diverge at the read layer (the Send panel page runs at plain admin, `aal2` defaults false; suppressions passes `aal2:true`) — SPLIT. (3) **W4 refuted "five verbs share a body"**: the repetition is silhouette, three already-extracted lines. **Guard integrity: H1's fixes HELD** — 14 of 15 prior findings genuinely pinned, 0 regressed, the five on invariant #3's gate chain closed; of 26 new-guard mutations **25 killed, 1 survived** — `latchHalt`'s `halted_at IS NULL` CAS (`approval.ts:479`), credited by three tests that never reach it because both arms refuse at the caller's state guard first. **Duplication:** the cancellable set has **SIX** spellings (the log said two) and `CONTEXT.md:75`'s own "a THIRD caller is the signal to extract" trigger has fired; `batchDidClose` is spelled 4× in 2 forms and that split already falsified `ApprovalPanel.tsx:562-563`; the purge writer and verifier share **seven** hand-typed sentinel literals. **New bug found (X9):** `suppressions-service.ts:72` runs a 2-wide `Promise.all` on the singleton `sql` against `DB_POOL_MAX=3`, contradicting `admission.ts:26-31` by name, missed because four fan-out pins enumerate their subjects. **Meta-class (X10):** four independent guards whose scope is an ENUMERATION — `ci:tenant-scope`, `ci:admin-aal2`, `design-scope-purity` (hence `auth-island.css:5-15`, Island palette redeclared outside every watched directory **with the fonts already diverged**), and the fan-out pins. **F9:** the OR-chain is **28** predicates, not 27; `tracked_keywords:144` uses `<>` where the identical column class at `:120` uses `IS DISTINCT FROM`. **P6, found by this pass ON this pass:** the Stop hook demanded the orphaned import left by a live mutation be fixed — and the obvious fix permanently deletes an invariant-#3 posting precondition. **Follow-up rate for the window: ZERO** — no product merge shipped a defect a later PR had to repair; residual risk has moved entirely to composition (staging-only) and to the apparatus itself, which has no layer that reviews it. 7 handoffs H1–H7. |
.claude/reference/arch-review-log.md:1407:| 2026-08-26 | #967 fix (single PR, not a pass — one of four triage findings; the other three were documentation or tracker-only) | `worker/ingress/resend/solicitation-lane.ts` (unmatched-attribution policy + payload-recipient fallback), `worker/jobs/account-offboarding/purge-stages.ts` (KNOWN GAP → CLOSED), `CONTEXT.md` (**Solicitation lane** re-anchored), the lane's live-DB suite (+9 cases, 43 green), `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-28-send-mode-executor-approval-design.md` (D9 veto-anchor amendment) | The purge's suppression contract promised a recipient's GLOBAL opt-out survives an account purge; for one recipient class it could not. `loadAttribution` joins our own `solicitation_contacts` row and the purge deletes it, so a post-purge bounce threw, retried until the 300s signature window 401'd it, and left the opt-out unwritten at `status='failed'`. **Retiring the retry was the owner's call on the measured shape of the problem:** a retry closes only ONE of three unmatched causes, and the other two are permanent — the purge, and a send whose terminal CAS lost (`dispatch.ts` `commitSendTerminal`) and never persisted `provider_message_id` at all. Suppression-bearing events now write the global row from the SIGNED payload with `accountId: null` — the contract's boundary rule stated exactly — and ack; soft bounces and `email.failed` are unchanged (§3.2 intact). **Exactly one address in `to`, or throw**: a global row blocks that person for every tenant, so the lane refuses to guess. Two costs accepted and recorded at the call site: the seconds-wide #630 race loses the outreach `bounced_at` stamp, so the **Send breaker** undercounts one bounce; and the acked payload's recipient address is bounded only by `ArchivalPoller`'s 30-day sweep of `processed` rows — itself a gain, since the old `failed` rows escaped that sweep entirely and retained an address forever. The `:836` normalization invariant is **narrowed, not retired**: while attribution exists the stored contact handle still wins and the payload is never read. Alongside, doc-only: D9's veto anchor recorded as the shipped `MIN(sent_at)` with `failed_at IS NULL`, not `delivered_at` (Telegram returns no delivery receipt) — owner-approved at build, never written down until now. **Process note:** the gate's `reclassify` row fired at 211 vs 90 estimated production lines; measurement showed no sprawl (5 of 5 declared files, one seam, ~64 executable lines added, 55% of the lane's additions being comment in a file already 55% comment), the estimate was corrected in both intake copies and the SMALL PATH held. |
.claude/reference/arch-review-log.md:1410:| 2026-08-26 | **12 counted merges ≥ 5 threshold** across a 21-merge window after `72dc58ac` (the marketing/landing wave #953/#955/#959/#968/#976; the solicitation attribution + suppression trio #954/#964/#975; the three 08-18 carry-forwards #962/#970/#972; plus #969). **The counter itself read 8** | Pathfinder pass, **windowed** (owner's call): 8 features charted — F1 landing composition root, F2 landing motion primitives, F3 landing sections, F6 Island design system, F7 Daylight marketing pages, F8 solicitation attribution, F9 suppression & unsubscribe, F10 ask dispatch, F11 purge & verification. **664 nodes**, every node `file:line`-cited. Three features (F12/F13/F14) recorded as no-chart — comment-only in this window. Plus a cross-feature duplication axis and a **46-guard scope census**. Artifacts `docs/reviews/PATHFINDER-2026-08-26/00-09` | **Headline: the enumerated-scope guard class the 08-18 pass NAMED produced FIVE new findings two windows later, and the pass's own handoffs INVERTED — 3-of-3 landed from 08-18, 0-of-3 from 08-24.** **Guard census, 46 mechanical guards:** 18 Class A (pure enumeration), **25 Class S** — a class this pass names: *derived* discovery **narrowed by a hand-written scan root** — 4 Class C, and **only 6 that detect an EMPTY scan**. Class S is bigger than Class A and is the real problem; `ci:pool-fanout` proves it — the #505 fan-out pins did not disappear when they became a rule, they **became `SCAN_DIRS`**. **NOT the same four guards** as 08-18: one identical, three descended, two new — **the class has grown**. New failure mode named: **exemption transit** — `owner_leads`'s CORRECT Class-B exemption at `tenant-tables.ts:210` silently became an OMISSION in `table-disposition.test.ts`'s required set; nobody erred, and 08-22's proposed two-line `linkedColumnPattern` fix would NOT have caught it. General fix in two steps, **cheaper than the `ci:guard-scope` meta-audit 08-22 deferred and strictly wider**: a `scannedCount === 0` fatal in `ratchet-harness.ts`, plus exporting every `SCAN_DIRS` with one `ci-audit-wiring` case failing on a directory zero audits cover. **The counter is wrong for the SIXTH consecutive pass and this file's own prescribed fix is UNSOUND** — `ci:merge-ledger` fires on production OR governance while the rule counts production only, so #957/#960/#961 were each required to add a line and must not increment; "count the lines" over-counts by construction. The 08-24 pass credited `ci:merge-ledger` with counter correctness; that audit's header explicitly declines the job. **First pass where the MARKETING surface, not the pipeline, is the largest changed area** — `src/components/` took 51% of the window's net growth; 100 files / 17,141 lines, 46% CSS, never charted before. **This log's own CSS claim REFUTED:** `agent-flip-card.css` is import **#1**, not last; there are **three** unguarded order dependencies, not two, and the one that IS guarded (`globals.css:186-189` via `design-scope-purity.test.ts:39-45`) got no credit. **Arrival grammar has SIX spellings of one idea**, four live — proven one system by `carousel.css:112-113` neutralising all three Landing variants with a single `!important`. **Largest duplication measured in six passes:** the `businesses ⋈ accounts` subscription read is **33 sites**, byte-identical predicate, no fragment and no comment — and it **corrects this pass's own F8 flowchart**, which reported five, one a false positive. **#892's verdict QUALIFIED:** #972 owned the tombstone sentinels and stopped one literal class short — writer and verifier still hand-share `'scrubbed:'` ×20 split 10↔10, and because the verifier is a **fail-closed compliance gate**, verifier-side drift converts a failed purge into a **PASS**. **Live defects, each with reachability answered SEPARATELY:** `ProblemSection.tsx:47` branches on `usePrefersReducedMotion` with no mount gate, so every reduced-motion visitor gets the video branch until hydration — and `HeroSection.tsx:48-56`'s own docstring names the bug, having solved it twice privately without extracting it (MEDIUM; `preload="none"` mitigates); `owner_leads` retains owner PII through an account purge; `contacts-repo.ts:103` runs the two-way `Promise.all` #893 reverted elsewhere; `/pricing` freezes `isFoundingWindowOpen()` at build (`pricing/page.tsx:17`) while checkout evaluates at request — **date-bounded, cannot fire before 2027-01-01**. **H3's ordering constraint was VIOLATED** — #633 flipped send-mode on staging and the doc gate never landed; the only two autonomy flags ON in the deployed estate are the two no runbook mentions, the documented "instant kill switch" `AUTO_APPROVAL_ENABLED=false` has **zero reads** in that lane, and a third file H3 never listed — `beta-production-standup.md:143`, the **production** checklist — omits both. **Production risk zero, every flag unset.** **08-24's H1 and H2 confirmed present but re-classified LATENT** (`auto-policy-publish.ts:555-562` + measured Railway flag state) — their prompts' present tense was wrong and is corrected. **F8, the newest subsystem (#954, migration 114), passes EVERY invariant** — outbox, explicit-client, tenant-scope, idempotency, `ON CONFLICT` matching its partial index byte-for-byte. **Seed 6 REFUTED twice independently:** all four locked suppression terms hold. **Migration 114 lockstep verified by introspecting BOTH databases**; the 078 standing exception shows its exact documented prod signature. Gates 21/21 (audit count 20→21 with `ci:env-registry`); `pnpm test` and `ci:fallow:coverage` NOT run — test health at HEAD unmeasured, and no guard-integrity mutation axis this pass. **Method note: the "a citation is not a verification" rule caught an error in the ORCHESTRATOR's own work** — a `head -12` truncation hid the `/pricing` call site and nearly produced a false refutation of a real finding. 9 DO-NOT-UNIFY additions. 10 handoffs H1–H10; `#3a` deliberately NOT carried a third time —