.claude/reference/arch-review-log.md:1411:| 2026-08-26 | feat-qr-review-request (single PR via /feature, RISK=high — roadmap Phase 0 pull-forward, owner decision 2026-08-26) | migration 115 + `events.ts`/`events.test.ts`/`docs/analytics/events.md` (`qr_scan_redirected`), `subscription-status.ts` (+`subscriptionAllowsQrRedirect`), `src/lib/locations/{review-qr.ts,repo.ts}` (+`getQrRedirectRow`), tenant-scope allowlist (+1 `pre-auth-token`, baseline 370), public `src/app/q/[businessId]/route.ts`, `/settings/review-qr` section + print view + `SettingsSidebar` entry, 7 test files carrying the intake's 18 promised titles (2 new live-DB suites), the 106 drift guard handed to a new 115 suite | **Review QR** (CONTEXT.md): per-location printable QR encoding the RepWorth-owned **QR redirect** `/q/<businessId>`, 302 to Google's write-review deep link. Gate = `{active, trialing, past_due}` via the named predicate (owner decision — `past_due` keeps a printed counter code alive mid-grace); every refusal (bad id, missing row, archived, `pending_payment`/`cancelled`, non-canonical place id) serves one byte-identical scanner page, reason-coded in the log only. The destination is CONSTRUCTED from an `isPlaceId`-validated place id — no stored URL, no open redirect, hex CIDs refused (the `buildReviewLink` precedent). Scan counting is a best-effort `qr_scan_redirected` insert AFTER resolve: random event key per scan (a deterministic key would dedupe on `ON CONFLICT` and undercount), ids duplicated into properties because `AnalyticsDispatchPoller` ships only the properties JSON. Plan hardened through three codex plan-review rounds — two orchestrator rejections REVERSED on codex evidence (settings component tests are house standard; the sidebar test exists), two codex factual claims corrected in return, one orchestrator rationale (file-granular allowlist) disproven by codex running the audit — full record in the plan's review appendix + deviations file. Migration 115 stays LOCAL-ONLY unti