.claude/reference/arch-review-log.md:1420:| 2026-08-29 | Refusal Log — one vocabulary + one owner-safe read + the Restraint tab (`/feature`, RISK=high) | NEW `src/lib/refusals/{vocabulary,read}.ts`, NEW `src/app/api/dashboard/refusals/route.ts`, NEW `src/components/dashboard/analytics/AnalyticsTabs.tsx` + `…/dashboard/analytics/restraint/{page.tsx,restraint.css}`, both analytics views, `src/lib/agents/read.ts` (scope rename `AgentTeamScope` → `DashboardReadScope`), `CONTEXT.md` (4 LOCKED terms), ADR 0023 | **No migration — 116 stayed unused.** Every reason was already persisted; the work was projection, not capture. **Four factual corrections to the brief's premise, each verified in code rather than taken on report:** (1) `judge_verdicts` is NOT a refusal — the Judge runs on already-posted replies (`judge-store.ts:115`, `WHERE r.status = 'posted'`), so counting one would be false AND would double-count the autonomy suspension a flag triggers; dropped, which halved the deny-all read surface. (2) Autonomy suspension re-sourced from `auto_approval_policies` to `account_audit_log` — `unsuspendAccountAutonomy` NULLs both policy columns (`suspension.ts:352-354`), so the policy row holds no history and the approved behaviour "a lifted suspension still appears" was unbuildable as planned. (3) `solicitation_outreach`'s withheld arm has TWO writers with two different correct timestamps, so the anchor is reason-dependent — `rendered_at` for the three `RenderWithholdReason` codes, `COALESCE(run.started_at, updated_at)` for the other five; neither is correct alone, and `updated_at` alone can drift. (4) `admin_halt`/`platform_halt` are stored twice — `latchHalt` copies a batch halt through to every cancelled Outreach row — so the outreach copies map to `null`, or one halt is reported again per recipient. **Stated limit, deliberately not closed:** `AutoApprovalBlockReason` (22 members) reaches only a `logger.log` at `persist.ts:570-576`, so the log reports THAT a draft was held for the owner, never WHY — probably the highest-volume refusal in the system. ADR 0023 owns that sentence; closing it needs a capture change and only fills forward from deploy. **One eval defect worth remembering:** collapsing six scoped queries into one `UNION ALL` made per-arm tenant isolation unprovable by structural SQL assertion — predicates existing *anywhere* in the combined statement satisfied it — so every arm now carries its own behavioural foreign-account/foreign-location negative-row test, each proved non-vacuous by mutation (dropping the `businesses` bridge → 4 audit findings; joining account-wide S4 through locations → 6 failures; collapsing either half of the S6 anchor → 2 and 4). Also caught pre-merge: `vocabulary.ts` briefly value-imported `@/lib/approval/audit`, whose graph reaches `node:crypto`, which would have entered the browser bundle through `'use client'` label consumers with no ESLint rule to catch that pair. Plan review ran the full 3 rounds, findings converging 24 → 4 → 1. |
docs/reviews/feat-qr-review-request/standards-round1.md:60:2. **Deep-module discipline.** `src/lib/locations/review-qr.ts` is a genuinely deep module: two async entry points + one pure builder + two result types; refusal ordering, eligibility, QR parameters, and the accounts-JOIN authority all hidden behind `QrRedirectResolution` / `OwnerReviewQrLocation`. `resolveQrRedirect` is a pure-result seam (route owns 302/page/log/insert) — no pass-throughs, nothing fails the deletion test. `getQrRedirectRow` lives in `repo.ts` per that file's ownership header, correctly. The one interface widen is test-only (`buildWriteReviewUrl` export — see A2, dissolved by F1's remedy).
