.claude/reference/lab-notes.md:20:- **Solicitation / CSV ingest** — the `csv_ingest` advisory-lock contract covers status transitions only: the offboarding purge hard-DELETEs `contact_csv_uploads` unlocked, so `writeTerminalUploadState` deliberately TOLERATES a 0-row terminal write rather than asserting (#582); the batch builder pools every contact of the business, so a staging smoke's funnel never equals its own CSV; `useReviewedPing` is `visibilityState`-gated so background automation never writes `reviewed_at`; the Suppression ledger's §1.2 lookup has ONE owner (`suppressionMatchSql`) and its `channel` is a PARAMETER on both reader and writer — a hardcoded literal on one side fails OPEN the day the channel enum grows (#643); the offboarding token scrub matches on `account_id` alone so its account-leading index is usable, with the `business_id` arm kept only in the purge VERIFIER as a cross-account tripwire
.claude/reference/lab-notes.md:23:- **False coverage / mutation** — a test that passes whether or not the bug exists is the dominant defect mode on guard-shaped work; a fix for an "X is untested" finding must ITSELF be mutation-pinned or it reproduces the defect (happened twice in consecutive rounds at #679, and ~10 instances there were caught by mutation, none by reading); a JS `throw` does not poison a Postgres transaction, so savepoint-recovery tests need Postgres-side abort injection (#679, 2026-08-08); **Testing-Library's `rerender` PRESERVES component state, so it structurally cannot prove an UNMOUNT defect** — two promised tests passed against a panel that reset the owner's deselections on every refetch, through a full review round; a test for state that must SURVIVE a refetch belongs in the PARENT's suite driving the real mount boundary (#860, 2026-08-18); **a fail-open guard needs an oracle for the OPEN half** — pinning only the refusal left `budgetRemaining: null` (Redis down) undefended, and `(x ?? 0) <= 0` type-checks, keeps 29/30 green, and converts an Upstash outage into a dead lane (#860, 2026-08-18); **an all-or-nothing CHECK forces combined-restore tests, and a SQL-shape assertion then proves only that a predicate is PRESENT, never that its COMPARISON is right** — `IS DISTINCT FROM 'wrong literal'` satisfies `toContain` while detecting nothing, and a sibling column's violation carries the count; isolate each column (restore alone → expect 1 → revert → expect 0, labelled per column) wherever no constraint forbids it (#665, 2026-08-18); **a lint-on-stop hook cannot tell a MEASUREMENT from a mistake** — with a guard deleted on purpose, ESLint reports the orphaned import and its mechanically obvious remedy (delete the import) removes the guard PERMANENTLY, which is how invariant #3's auto-policy conjunct was nearly lost mid-census; declare the mutation with `touch .feature/mutation-in-progress` (git-ignored) — BOTH `.claude/hooks/` and `.codex/hooks/typecheck-on-stop.sh` then skip the eslint block only, typecheck still runs, and no green stamp is written — and remove it the moment the file is restored (#896, 2026-08-23)
.claude/reference/lab-notes.md:26:- **Owner offboarding** — `railway up` from a worktree ships stale worker code (`OutboxPoller: Unknown topic`); Stripe Basil/Dahlia moved `current_period_end` onto the subscription item; `approval_audit_log` has no `approval_link_id`/`user_agent` (mock-asserted SQL *text* hid the drift); keep-my-data must be exempt from the blanket `/api/account/*` owner-API proxy gate; the `purge_after` token-expiry trigger blocks shrinking the purge window while a keep-my-data token is live; **the purge VERIFIER is a gate, not a report** — it throws inside `finalizePurgeInTransaction`, so a blind predicate is an open gate and a newly-strict one BLOCKS a legitimate purge, and its `businesses` residue list has two shapes ("was cleared" vs "was set to X"), the second of which needs `IS DISTINCT FROM` on a nullable column or a nulled value passes silently — `archived_at IS NULL` is the only predicate that can catch a row the tombstone never touched at all (#665, 2026-08-18)
