docs/currents.md:3596:This was **specced, built across 7 PRs, dry-run-tested on staging, and fixed before merge.** The staging dry-run caught three real bugs that unit tests had hidden — cancel-only never scheduling, the keep-my-data link 401'ing logged-out owners, and the delete purge failing on phantom columns — all fixed (PR #245) and then **re-run live on staging end-to-end** (2026-06-09) before merging to `main`. The whole feature stays **off in production** behind `ACCOUNT_OFFBOARDING_ENABLED` until the legal terms (a non-refundable mid-cycle clause) are in place. One ops note: deploy the worker from a **clean checkout**, not `railway up` from a worktree — that ships stale code.
