docs/directory.md:84:| `u/[token]/page.tsx` | **(#644)** The recipient unsubscribe landing page. Three states from one URL: the **button page** (names the originating business, or "the business that contacted you" when provenance was purged), the **success page**, and the **Neutral page** — one identical render for unknown, malformed *and* already-redeemed tokens, so no caller can tell them apart (§5.4). Success requires a verifying Success receipt **and** a live global suppression read **during that render**: a receipt proves a row existed when it was minted, and the Correction path can remove it inside the 10-min TTL. Plain `<form method="post">`, no client component — it works with JS disabled. |
docs/directory.md:127:| `dashboard/requests/lane-writes.ts` | **(#886; the section is #629's, moved)** The approval lane's WRITE seam, split out of `ApprovalPanel.tsx` when that file crossed 1,000 lines (982 → 1,109; only ~94 of them #872's). Owns `useLaneWrites` — approve, halt, regenerate, withdraw over ONE settle path — plus `postLaneAction`, the `LaneStatus` union taken from the four route result types (so a new refusal is a `tsc` error here rather than silent generic copy), `LANE_REFUSAL_COPY` + `NOT_REGENERABLE_COPY`, the four `Announce` sentences, and `countPhrase`. **`LaneWriteOutcome` and `LaneRefresh` are exported from HERE, not from the panel** — they are the write's vocabulary, and `RequestsClient` imports them from here. Traps: (a) the seam is the four verbs and nothing else — `useExcludedAsks`, `usePendingRegeneration` and `useArmedWithdrawal` stay in the panel because they are about what is on SCREEN, not what is on the WIRE; (b) nothing here refetches — `onChanged` is the parent's cue and the `LaneRefresh` each verb passes says which kind (`replace` for the two terminal verbs, `in_place` for the two that come back to the same panel); (c) `countPhrase` moved WITH the section because the panel's prose reads it too, and leaving it behind would make this module import from its own importer. |
docs/directory.md:217:| `offboardings/page.tsx` | **(Phase 3)** Server component: gate with **`aal2: true`** (parity with `GET /api/admin/offboardings`' `requireAdminWithAal2`), `getAdminOffboardings`, `<AdminPage group="Businesses">`. |
docs/directory.md:218:| `offboardings/OffboardingsClient.tsx` | **(Phase 3)** Client island: offboarding lifecycle cards, provider-disposition mutation, shared `PaginationFooter`; owns `PAGE_SIZE` and the tone-keyed `ToneBadge` (renamed from a local `StatusBadge` that shadowed the shared primitive). |
docs/directory.md:359:| `solicitation/batch/halt/route.ts` | **(#629)** POST: the owner stops a batch through the **Halt latch**. Same shape as `approve`, reading **only** `batchId` — the halt reason is derived server-side from **Batch state** by `ownerHaltReason` and is never accepted, forwarded, or defaulted from the client, because a client that could name its own reason could file a mid-drip halt as a veto and make the audit trail lie about whether email had left. halted/already_halted → 200, not_haltable → 409, not_found → 404. Its cross-origin refusal is pinned by a test on purpose: halt is as destructive as approval and must not be the one verb whose CSRF guard is unasserted. |
docs/directory.md:371:**(#656)** PUT: records the **Attested postal address** for the owner's cookie-resolved active location. Auth is `resolveOwnerScope` (NOT `requireSettingsOwner`, which resolves no location and deliberately skips the writable-subscription gate) plus `withSameOrigin()`, and an explicit `getOffboardingState`/`isOperationalUIBlocked` refusal placed **before the body parse** — the subscription gate does not imply it, since `delete_data`/`pending` is operationally blocked while the subscription is still `active`. `z.strictObject` is load-bearing: a body-supplied `businessId` or `userId` is a 400, never a silently ignored tenant-selection knob, and `attestationVersion` is pinned to the constant so a client can never assent to one text while the server records another. Delegates to `attestPostalAddress` and maps its four statuses to 200/400/403/404; the lint lives in the module, never here.
docs/directory.md:415:| `offboardings/route.ts` | GET the offboarding lifecycle list behind `requireAdminWithAal2`; delegates to `getAdminOffboardings`. Its page gate matches (`requireAdminPage(sql, {aal2: true})`). |
