docs/directory.md:728:| `request-path-header.ts` | Two constants: `REQUEST_PATHNAME_HEADER` (`x-repworth-pathname`) and `ACCOUNT_OFFBOARDING_STATUS_PATH` (`/account/offboarding/status`). |
docs/directory.md:731:| `session-cookie-secret.ts` | `getSessionCookieSecret()` — single authoritative reader of `SESSION_COOKIE_SECRET` (via `getServerConfig()`) for every HMAC consumer (approval device cookies, Zernio connect cookies, offboarding keep-my-data tokens, destructive fresh-auth); throws if unset or shorter than 32 bytes. |
docs/directory.md:788:| `settings.ts` | Server-owned read/write of `auto_approval_policies` (invariant #14 — browser code never touches the table): `getAutoApprovalSettings(db, { accountId, impersonated })` and `patchAutoApprovalSettings(sql, input)` behind `GET`/`PATCH /api/settings/auto-approval`. PATCH runs in one tx: account row `FOR UPDATE`, offboarding gate, before-state read, pure after-state, then archived-location → `standard` confirmation → readiness gates BEFORE any write, upsert/delete, `auto_approval_policy_changed` audit. Throws `AutoApprovalConfirmationRequiredError` / `AutoApprovalExpansionBlockedError` / `AutoApprovalSettingsError`. The Solicitation lane (#631 D20) lives in `solicitation-settings.ts` — this file keeps the public interface and joins to it at exactly two points: `updatePolicyInTransaction`'s solicitation branch (PATCH) and the GET response's `solicitation` block. |
