docs/progresstracking.md:245:**Status:** Feature COMPLETE and shipped to `main` **flag-OFF** (`ACCOUNT_OFFBOARDING_ENABLED` unset in prod — zero customer-facing change until ops enables it after the legal launch gate). End-to-end **verified live on staging** 2026-06-09. Plan: `~/.claude/grill-codex/20260605-214141/PLAN.md`; converged spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-05-owner-offboarding-design.md`; evidence record: `docs/runbooks/owner-offboarding-staging-dry-run.md`.
docs/progresstracking.md:249:- **`delete_data`** — stop processing immediately, cancel billing + revoke Zernio + archive locations at teardown-start, then a **30-day staged, resumable purge**; "keep my data" can cancel the purge (→ retained-data churn) but never undoes billing/provider teardown.
docs/progresstracking.md:255:| PR1 | `account_offboardings` + `account_offboarding_tokens` (migration **056**, deny-all RLS, `UNIQUE (account_id) WHERE terminal_at IS NULL`), the test-enforced **table-disposition inventory** (`src/lib/account-offboarding/table-disposition.ts` — CI fails on any unclassified account-linked table), and no-op shared guard helpers. |
