docs/progresstracking.md:263:**8-status machine:** `pending → scheduled → tearing_down → purge_scheduled → purged` with terminal branches `churned` / `reactivated` / `failed (+failed_step)`; every terminal stamps `terminal_at`. A `failed`/`failed_step='teardown'` row is re-driven by `TeardownRetryPoller` up to `…_TEARDOWN_MAX_RETRIES`, then held for an operator; a stale `reactivation_claimed_at` (>5 min) is released by `ReactivationResetPoller`.
docs/progresstracking.md:267:- **D2 — keep-my-data email link 401s logged-out owners.** The proxy's `isProtectedOwnerApiRoute` blanket-matched `/api/account/*` and trapped the public, token-authenticated `/api/account/offboarding/keep-my-data` — the primary rescue path returned 401.
docs/progresstracking.md:268:- **D3 — delete_data purge always failed; data never deleted.** The scrub + verification referenced `approval_audit_log` columns `approval_link_id` / `user_agent` that don't exist → purge threw at plan time, row stuck `failed/purge`. *Masked by:* unit tests asserting the scrub **SQL text** (incl. the phantom columns), never the real schema. A functional **and** compliance failure (deletion promised, not delivered).
docs/progresstracking.md:270:**Fixes (PR #245 → `owner-offboarding-plan`):** D1 → read `items.data[0].current_period_end ?? top-level`; D2 → a `PUBLIC_OWNER_ACCOUNT_API_PATHS` exemption (the route does its own token validation); D3 → drop the two phantom columns from the scrub + verification (the real PII columns incl. `response_text_at_approval` are still nulled; the sibling `user_agent`/`ip` scrub on `account_audit_log` is correct — that table really has those columns). Each got a regression test at the seam the mock drift hid: D1 feeds the real Basil item shape, D3 adds a **real-DB integration test** running the production scrub/verification against the real schema, D2 pins the route public.
docs/progresstracking.md:272:**Live UI E2E on fix-deployed staging (2026-06-09, Chrome DevTools):** deployed the fix branch to the full staging stack (Vercel staging custom env + Railway worker) and drove all three on a disposable account (real signup UI + Gmail OTP + Stripe **test-mode** checkout → active sub): **D1** cancel_only → `scheduled` (+ reactivation → `reactivated`), **D2** keep-my-data GET → 200 (was 401), **D3** delete_data → teardown → `purge_scheduled` → `purged` (account/user PII tombstoned). Recorded in the runbook (§0 "Live UI E2E").
docs/progresstracking.md:274:> **Deploy gotcha (operational, NOT a code defect):** the first worker deploy via `railway up` *from the nested git worktree* shipped **stale** worker code missing the offboarding queue wiring (`OutboxPoller: Unknown topic "account_offboarding_billing_schedule"`), stalling every offboarding job. Redeploying the worker from a **clean clone** fixed it. Deploy the staging/prod worker from a clean checkout, never `railway up` from `.claude/worktrees/*`.
docs/progresstracking.md:276:**Merge:** PR #245 squash-merged into `owner-offboarding-plan`, then PR #244 squash-merged into `main` (2026-06-09; CI green on both; `main` commit `22ba46c2`). Feature stays **dark in prod** (flag unset — merging code does not flip env vars).
