docs/progresstracking.md:375:| **B — auto-approved post FYI, end-to-end (#320, migration 067)** | New outbox topic `auto_post_notice` wired end-to-end (`queue-names`, `queues.ts`, `worker/index.ts`, snake_case `AutoPostNoticePayload`, **offboarding teardown terminalization**). Shared `markPostedAndMaybeEnqueueAutoPostNotice` called from **both** publisher success paths (fresh-2xx **and** the 409 text-match recovery), in one `sql.begin()`, with an affected-row guard (`UPDATE … RETURNING`, enqueue only on `count===1`) and `approval_method='auto_policy'` gate. New worker `worker/jobs/auto-post-notice/{AutoPostNoticeWorker,context,dispatch,errors}.ts` (separate from the approval dispatch; creates **zero** `approval_links`). New `sendAutoPostNotice` channel method returning a `sent`/`skipped` union (WhatsApp pre-filtered when its template SID is unset). **Claim-before-send** dedup (`notification_deliveries`, release on retryable / failed-row on terminal). Hardened public redirect `/r/google/[responseId]` (UUID + `status='posted'` join + Google host allowlist + `no-store` + unavailable page). FYI email template + `auto_post_notice` added to `OWNER_DIRECTED_TEMPLATES` (hard-bounce flags `owner_email_bounced`). Migration **067** = two partial unique indexes (in-flight outbox dedup + the claim dedup), additive/instant. |
docs/progresstracking.md:405:**Key decisions:** owner-approval-only beta (ADR 0005) — auto-approval go-live is a **separate** later gate (prod moderation validation + canary + kill-switch drill + FYI-failure paging); the probe targets **silent** failures only (post-hoc alerting can't prevent an irreversible auto-post, so that risk is carried by the human approval step); the alert sink is **Sentry → Discord**, mandatory non-email (admin email shares Resend with the product); the two cheap timeouts *gate* despite being small because at `concurrency:1` they're single points of stall; the 1000-scale work (worker concurrency / horizontal scale, circuit breakers, ArchivalPoller drain, etc.) is **deferred to growth triggers** in the worker-scaling backlog, not built for a 50-business reality. **Beta is subscription-invoices-only** (documented constraint) so the un-scoped `invoice.payment_failed` (backlog P4 #11) can't wrongly flip a paying account to `past_due`.
docs/progresstracking.md:421:3. **Webhook lifecycle** through the applier: `checkout.session.completed` (trial start), `customer.subscription.updated` + `invoice.paid` (convert → `active`, only when Stripe says `active` — the $0 trial-start invoice does NOT convert), `invoice.payment_failed` + new `invoice-payment-action-required.ts` (SCA → `past_due` + 7-day grace), `customer.subscription.deleted` (cancel via existing offboarding `cancel_at_period_end`).
docs/progresstracking.md:437:**Key decisions.** Card-up-front Stripe-native (reuses Checkout + webhooks; limits abuse on a real-cost product) · explicit `'trialing'` status (fails closed) over reusing `active` (fails open) · `subscription_activated_at` reused as the service-start anchor, NO new column · ranking excluded from trials (paid SerpAPI) as the one bound on "full product" · lean abuse posture (existing signup limits + Stripe card fingerprint; no repeat-trial blocker) · cancellation reuses existing offboarding `cancel_at_period_end`.
docs/progresstracking.md:494:1. **DB-singleton injection — the `105 → 0` arc (Residual A, closed permanently + structurally).** The ambient-DB-singleton importer set was ratcheted from **105 checked-in files** (Stage 1, #441, when `ci:db-imports` landed as a baseline guard) to **zero** (2i, #455) across nine domain sweeps (auth/approval, admin/accounts, billing/onboarding, KPI/dashboard, channels/notifications, reviews/responses/zernio, publishing, offboarding/locations, shared/app tail). Every business-logic module under `src/lib/**` + every worker helper now takes `sql`/`supabaseServer` (or `tx` inside a transaction) as an **explicit parameter**; only composition roots import `@/lib/db/server`. The **baseline was then deleted and the guard flipped STRICT** (PR 3, #456): worker root status is **derived from `worker/index.ts` registration** via TypeScript-AST parsing (not file position), `import type` excluded, unit-tested (11/11), CI-wired — regression is now structurally impossible. Only `src/lib/db/auth.ts` (owner-classified root) imports the singleton in `src/lib`.
docs/progresstracking.md:498:3. **Bonus single-source + guard hardening.** `ci:reviews-status` (strict) + `ci:outbox-topics` guards closed two June single-source residuals; new single-owner modules landed for the Q1 amplifiers (`src/components/ui/marketing-links.ts` for NAV/MARKETING links, `src/lib/shared/queue-health-states.ts`, `src/lib/reviews/status.ts` `REVIEW_STATUS`, `src/lib/account-offboarding/outbox.ts` for the offboarding enqueuers); `ci:process-env` widened; four fat routes extracted to thin+injected+test-pinned modules (Q3 → A).
