docs/reviews/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/plan-gate-codex-round1.md:12:5. **High** — T8 either releases the advisory lock before the protected work or introduces a lock-order deadlock. `prepareBatch` and `constructBatch` are separate transactions at [batch-builder:190](/Users/norbertesekiel/Developer/startups/RepWorth-worktrees/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/src/lib/solicitation/batch-builder.ts:190) and [batch-builder:579](/Users/norbertesekiel/Developer/startups/RepWorth-worktrees/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/src/lib/solicitation/batch-builder.ts:579). The current construction takes the batch-row lock before the advisory lock at [batch-builder:589](/Users/norbertesekiel/Developer/startups/RepWorth-worktrees/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/src/lib/solicitation/batch-builder.ts:589), while T8 moves the helper to `prepareBatch` and has purge take advisory locks before cascading deletes at [plan:286](/Users/norbertesekiel/Developer/startups/RepWorth-worktrees/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/docs/superpowers/plans/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout-plan.md:286). Fix: define one global lock order, keep the lock in the transaction it protects, align purge to that order, and add a concurrent build-versus-purge integration test.
docs/reviews/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/plan-gate-codex-round1.md:22:10. **High** — T6 performs an unbounded UPDATE. The plan updates every eligible body in one statement at [plan:261](/Users/norbertesekiel/Developer/startups/RepWorth-worktrees/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/docs/superpowers/plans/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout-plan.md:261), while every existing archival arm deliberately caps work at 5,000 rows, e.g. [ArchivalPoller:39](/Users/norbertesekiel/Developer/startups/RepWorth-worktrees/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/worker/background/pollers/ArchivalPoller.ts:39). A large first backlog can repeatedly hit statement timeout without making progress. Fix: use an ordered, bounded candidate CTE with `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, update by ID, and report saturation.
docs/reviews/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/plan-gate-codex-round1.md:36:17. **Medium** — The verification contract does not execute most promised behavior. Its commands run only the migration-shape suite and two audits at [intake:111](/Users/norbertesekiel/Developer/startups/RepWorth-worktrees/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/docs/superpowers/plans/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout-intake.json:111), omitting the concurrent-close suite, poller/offboarding tests, typecheck, and build. Fix: add explicit targeted suites plus typecheck/build, including the concurrent live-DB test.
docs/reviews/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/plan-gate-codex-round1.md:38:18. **Low** — The “Verified facts” table contains overstated wording and bad citations: “asks has only its PK and batch/contact” ignores its FKs and CHECKs ([088:160](/Users/norbertesekiel/Developer/startups/RepWorth-worktrees/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/supabase/migrations/088_solicitation_batch_executor.sql:160)); the outbox-topics scope citation points at blank line 52 instead of [outbox-topics-audit:23](/Users/norbertesekiel/Developer/startups/RepWorth-worktrees/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/scripts/ci/outbox-topics-audit.ts:23); and the lock-helper citation does not prove its purge import, which is at [purge-stages:11](/Users/norbertesekiel/Developer/startups/RepWorth-worktrees/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/worker/jobs/account-offboarding/purge-stages.ts:11). Fix the wording to “only unique constraints” and correct the citations.
