docs/reviews/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/adversarial-review-codex-raw.log:56:No-ship. The design embeds a deadlocking temporal contract, under-constrains both lifecycle models, and leaves purge/redaction safety dependent on future caller discipline.
docs/reviews/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/adversarial-review-codex-raw.log:60:  The documented contract requires callers to fail the send parent before closing. That takes the agent_runs lock first; closeBatchIfSettled takes the batch lock first and later locks agent_runs through recordStep/completeRun. A concurrent backstop or last-child close therefore forms run→batch versus batch→run. If PostgreSQL aborts the failure transaction, the closer can observe no error code, CAS send_closed_at, and record exhausted/completed. A retry cannot repair it because both closure and terminal run transitions subsequently no-op. This also disproves the NON_REVIEW_SUBJECT_CALLER justification that no run-lock holder waits on solicitation_batches.
docs/reviews/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/adversarial-review-codex-raw.log:62:- [high] The advisory lock does not protect an in-flight provider send from purge (worker/jobs/account-offboarding/purge-stages.ts:270-309)
docs/reviews/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/adversarial-review-codex-raw.log:63:  The purge takes the transaction-scoped advisory lock and then unconditionally deletes contact_csv_uploads, cascading through batches and outreach. Once #630 commits delivery_status='sending', its advisory lock is released before the provider call; purge can then acquire the lock and delete the committed sending row while that call is in flight. This is a real send-with-no-record gap, not solved by the advertised global lock order. The ADR assigns a future fix, but this primitive is unsafe by default for its intended consumer.
docs/reviews/feat-624-spine-lifecycle-fanout/adversarial-review-codex-raw.log:64:  Recommendation: After acquiring all advisory locks, have purge detect committed sending claims and durably defer/fail the purge until they resolve. Add a live race test covering claim commit, paused provider call, purge refusal, and terminal completion.
