docs/reviews/feat-674-import-review-no-generation/plan-round-3.md:47:  - Evidence: The review columns queried by the first test exist in the base schema or sentiment migration (`supabase/migrations/001_initial_schema.sql:155-182`; `supabase/migrations/052_reviews_sentiment.sql:8-11`). `agent_runs.account_id`, `kind`, `status`, and `ended_at` also exist (`supabase/migrations/071_agent_run_spine.sql:15-36`), and `analytics_events.account_id` exists (`supabase/migrations/046_analytics_events.sql:6-39`).
docs/reviews/feat-674-import-review-no-generation/plan-round-3.md:54:  - Evidence: Ignoring the `run_id` spelling failure already reported in check 5, the intended deletion order is FK-safe (`docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-05-674-import-review-no-generation.md:693-705`). `agent_run_steps.agent_run_id` references `agent_runs` with `ON DELETE CASCADE`, so deleting steps before runs is safe (`supabase/migrations/071_agent_run_spine.sql:49-62`). Runs reference accounts and businesses with cascading deletion (`supabase/migrations/071_agent_run_spine.sql:15-18`). Reviews reference businesses with cascading deletion, and responses reference reviews and businesses with cascading deletion (`supabase/migrations/001_initial_schema.sql:155-158`, `supabase/migrations/001_initial_schema.sql:187-191`). Analytics references accounts/businesses with `ON DELETE SET NULL`, and is deleted first anyway (`supabase/migrations/046_analytics_events.sql:25-30`). Businesses are deleted before their account, satisfying the restrictive business-to-account FK (`supabase/migrations/034_multi_location_schema.sql:285-296`). Finally, the account/user pair is deleted under deferred circular constraints by the shared cleanup helper (`src/lib/shared/__tests__/live-db-tenant.ts:71-84`; `supabase/migrations/036_defer_circular_fks.sql:1-13`).
