docs/reviews/PATHFINDER-2026-08-10/01-flowcharts/f3-on-demand-generation.md:30:**Generate happy path.** `POST /api/dashboard/reviews/[reviewId]/generate` (`generate/route.ts:145`, same-origin wrapped) is a pure composition root. Order is fixed: owner auth (`:42`) → **rate limit first** (`enforceDashboardRegenRateLimit`, `:47`, per-account burst 10/60s + hour 30/hr on distinct Redis keys, fails open) → tenant proof (`:54`, review must join a non-archived business under the caller's account — never the location cookie) → writable/offboarding pre-check (`:80`, one guard: `assertWritableSubscriptionForAccount` resolves offboarding in the same query) → **budget peek second** (`enforceRegenBudgetForReview`, `:90`, read-only advisory MGET of `regen:{reviewId}:{date}`, consumes nothing, fails open) → `sql.begin(onDemandGenerateTx)` (`:94`).
docs/reviews/PATHFINDER-2026-08-10/01-flowcharts/f3-on-demand-generation.md:36:**Regenerate door.** `POST /api/dashboard/past-replies/draft` (`draft/route.ts:266`), two modes. Gates: `resolveEditReplyScope` (`:70`) — which is where **`EDIT_REPLIES_ENABLED` gating lives** (`edit-reply-request.ts:56`, 503 `feature_disabled`); the Generate door has no such gate — then `assertCanEditReply` tier+ownership (`:85`), mode-dependent offboarding gate (`:92`–`:98`: regenerate=processing-class, manual=operational-UI-class), and the shared rate limiter for **regenerate mode only** (`:102`–`:105`; manual is a plain INSERT). **Notably absent: the `enforceRegenBudgetForReview` peek** — this door relies solely on the worker's authoritative `checkRegenBudget` (and regenerate rows are always `version > 1`, so the budget always arms). In-tx (`:108`): review lock (`:111`), resume-existing-draft branch (`:131` — held check `hasOpenFlag` `:153` → 409 `held_for_review`, else 409 `draft_already_exists` with resume payload), in-flight outbox guard (`:172`), `validateOptimisticConcurrency` (`:185`, absent from the Generate door — there is no live reply to be concurrent with), version MAX+1 (`:205`), then manual INSERT (`:229`) or `enqueueGenerateResponse` with `origin_lane='regenerate'` + `suppressNotification=true` (`:245`). Same worker consumes both lanes; all three doors (Generate, dashboard `/regenerate` at `regenerate/route.ts`, past-replies Regenerate) share the one per-account rate counter and the one per-review budget counter.
