docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-09-multi-location-hardening-design.md:12:| Spec scope | Launch-gating set: the 7 pre-launch fixes + price-change guard + full E2E kit. Fast-follow items (cost ceilings, LocationContext prop sync, `placeIdVerified` trust, offboarding Zernio-snapshot leaks, aggregate-view accuracy nits, doc drift) are explicitly **out of scope** — separate later spec. |
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-09-multi-location-hardening-design.md:35:1. **Race-proof archive (owner path)** — the shared `applyArchiveLocationUpdate` helper in `src/lib/locations/archive-location-tx.ts` (used by both the owner path and the teardown path) gains an explicit `blockPrimary` parameter: the owner path passes `true` (UPDATE gains `AND is_primary = FALSE`), the offboarding-teardown path passes `false` — archiving the primary there is intentional. The primary check branches on the **locked snapshot**, not the UPDATE rowcount: `lockArchiveContext` additionally selects and returns `is_primary`, and the `blockPrimary`-gated `promote_first` throw lives in the owner-path caller, after the existing `last_active_location` check (the helper is shared with teardown, which must not throw it; guard priority preserved). A 0-row UPDATE from a concurrent already-archived race still surfaces as `location_archive_conflict`, not a mislabeled `promote_first`.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-09-multi-location-hardening-design.md:37:3. **Reactivation self-heals** — `reactivateLocationTransaction`: first take the `accounts` row `FOR UPDATE` (it currently takes no account lock; same accounts → businesses lock ordering as archive/promote), then if the account has no active primary, promote the reactivated location to primary **in the same transaction** — silently, with a `writeAccountAuditLog` row in-tx and a flag in the API response (no new UI pre-launch). Heals the offboarding-cancel → reactivate flow automatically.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-09-multi-location-hardening-design.md:148:Account-level LLM cost ceilings (per-business daily caps scale linearly with location count); `LocationContext` prop re-sync; server-side `placeIdVerified` validation (the URL-mode `validate_place_id` enqueue itself is IN scope — Fix 7.5); offboarding Zernio-snapshot leaks (archived-location Zernio IDs excluded from teardown snapshot; connect-during-cancel-window escape); aggregate-view accuracy nits (`billingPending` index shift, sampled pending counts, status-literal duplication); auto-approval override warning on reactivation; migrations-log §5 doc drift; dropping the deprecated per-business digest columns.
