docs/security-audit/2026-06-15-refresh-delta.md:7:**Why a refresh:** The baseline audit predates ~4 weeks of feature work — owner-facing channels (Telegram/WhatsApp), multi-location, admin impersonation, account offboarding, the auto-post FYI. This pass re-runs the core rounds against current code, confirms the baseline remediations, and probes the new surfaces.
docs/security-audit/2026-06-15-refresh-delta.md:61:**Cross-round patterns:** Pattern A (boot assertions) — broadly implemented (Stripe, mock-mode, admin-email, channel, offboarding, Zernio asserts all present). Pattern B (sanitize at persistence boundary) — implemented for owner edit text. **Pattern C — PARTIAL (verified 2026-06-15):** a `beforeSend → scrubSentryEvent` scrubber now runs in all three runtimes and redacts sensitive *keys* in `extra`/`headers`/`data` (the log-PII half is done; channel inbound redaction is solid — see F-8 for the one exception), **but the breadcrumb + URL-value half of R5 M-3 is still open → F-7.**
docs/security-audit/2026-06-15-refresh-delta.md:68:**Where:** Gated WITH step-up (`requireAdminWithAal2`, `src/lib/auth/admin-mfa-gate.ts`): `impersonation/{start,end}`, `offboardings`, `offboardings/[id]/provider-disposition`, `billing/grant-extension`, `flagged`, `businesses/[id]/zernio-queue`.
docs/security-audit/2026-06-15-refresh-delta.md:153:- **Admin impersonation & account offboarding:** Both gated by `requireAdminWithAal2` + same-origin; offboarding destructive auth uses HMAC fresh-auth stamps + `safeHexCompare` (`timingSafeEqual`). In good shape.
