docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-544-watch-mode-batch-ui.md:91:1b. **All three reads run in ONE read-only `REPEATABLE READ` transaction.** One statement is not sufficient once the reads are plural: account-offboarding purge (`worker/jobs/account-offboarding/purge-stages.ts:243`) can delete the batch or its asks between Q1 and Q3, which would render a "built" batch with zero asks — a legitimate-looking screen describing a batch that no longer exists. Revision 2 rejected this on the grounds that the single-statement rewrite made it unnecessary; that reasoning covered Q3's internal consistency but not Q1-versus-Q3, and it was wrong.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-544-watch-mode-batch-ui.md:424:**Accessibility acceptance criteria** (all required, all tested): each reason group is a section with a semantic heading; the funnel is a `<ol>`, not divs; every interactive target ≥44px; visible focus ring on all focusables; no colour-only encoding of `velocity_banked` vs refusals (chip carries text); text contrast ≥4.5:1 in both themes; any animation respects `prefers-reduced-motion`.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-544-watch-mode-batch-ui.md:657:| 2 | Rev 2's rejection of the transaction finding was wrong: Q1 and Q3 are still separate, and offboarding purge (`purge-stages.ts:243`) can delete a batch between them, rendering a "built" batch with zero asks | All reads now run in one `REPEATABLE READ, READ ONLY` transaction |
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-544-watch-mode-batch-ui.md:681:**Carried into execution as an unverified pattern** (not a defect, but the first of its kind in this repo): `rg` finds zero prior uses of `ISOLATION LEVEL` / `REPEATABLE READ` / `SERIALIZABLE` anywhere in the codebase. T1's `REPEATABLE READ, READ ONLY` wrapper must be **proven** against the live staging pool during T1 step 9 — Supabase runs PgBouncer in transaction pooling mode, where CLAUDE.md already documents one silent no-op in this neighbourhood (`SELECT … FOR UPDATE` outside `sql.begin()`). If the isolation level does not actually take effect, say so and re-plan the purge-race fix rather than shipping a wrapper that reads as protection but isn't.
