docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-01-suppression-ledger-core.md:870:**Concurrency contract, stated because it is not enforced (review round 1, finding 12).** Content purge, tombstone and finalize are separate transactions (`PurgeWorker.ts:72-89`); finalize locks only the outbox row. A `recordSuppression` landing between the purge stage and this count would be omitted from the receipt, and one landing after verification could leave post-purge residue. **This is not reachable today** — `recordSuppression` has zero production callers (G6) — so the fix is a documented contract, not machinery:
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-01-suppression-ledger-core.md:872:> **Boundary states, named explicitly.** A suppression writer MUST NOT write a `scope='account'` row for an account whose `account_offboardings.status` is any **active teardown** state — `purge_scheduled` included — not merely a terminal one. `purge_scheduled` is precisely the window in which purge runs, and verification completes *before* the transition to `purged`, so a writer gated on "terminal" would sail straight through it. A global row written after the boundary MUST carry `accountId: null`, so it is retained without re-introducing account provenance the purge just removed.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-01-suppression-ledger-core.md:880:Add the field to the `purge_receipt` payload type in `worker-types.ts` (the block at `:266-268` already documents that `purge_receipt` carries its own data because the account row is scrubbed — extend that comment). Add the parameter to the enqueue helper in `outbox.ts`. Read it back in `AccountOffboardingEmailWorker`'s `purge_receipt` fork at `:219` and pass it to the template.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-01-suppression-ledger-core.md:882:Snapshot-at-purge, not query-at-send: a retried send must render a stable number, and the email worker must stay ignorant of the solicitation domain.
