docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-20-settings-ia-optimization.md:7:**Architecture:** A new nested `/settings/layout.tsx` owns a persistent `SettingsSidebar` (active item from `usePathname()`), so every settings page renders only its own content + `TopBar`. The legacy flag-off layout is retired — `MULTI_LOCATION_ENABLED` must stay `true` in prod. `/settings` server-redirects to `/settings/voice`; the voice route is un-gated so single-location accounts reach it. The current `AccountPanel` is split: business-profile fields → `ProfilePanel` (`/settings/profile`), subscription/quota/tier-change → `BillingPanel` (`/settings/billing`). The unified `AccountOffboardingPanel` is split by category — **Cancel subscription** → Billing, **Delete data** → Profile — both reading one shared `useOffboardingStatus()` hook; the DB's `UNIQUE(account_id) WHERE terminal_at IS NULL` one-active-offboarding constraint keeps the two panels coherent across routes.
