docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-03-656-postal-address-attestation.md:268:> **One documented exception: `rejects an address that fails the lint`.** `attestPostalAddress` **is** the linter — it takes the RAW address precisely so no code path can store an unlinted one — so the module is reached by design and returns `{ status: 'invalid' }` before its own UPDATE. Satisfying the zero-writes letter here would mean re-implementing the lint in the handler: a second author for one fact, and a violation of invariant #12. That test instead asserts (a) 400 carrying the **real** lint reason, (b) the **raw** address reached the module unchanged — proving the route neither pre-lints nor normalizes — and (c) a lint-clean address through the identical handler returns 200, so the 400 is the lint's verdict and not a hard-coded refusal. The other eight rejections do assert `not.toHaveBeenCalled()`. *(Found by T4; the unqualified rule was wrong.)*
