docs/superpowers/plans/refactor-565-complexity-bundle-intake.json:25:    "csv_ingest concurrency contract: every transaction that performs a contact_csv_uploads STATUS TRANSITION takes the per-business advisory lock as its FIRST statement, using the SAME key. This does NOT extend to every writer of the table — worker/jobs/account-offboarding/purge-stages.ts:256 hard-DELETEs by account_id without the lock, which is why the ingest 0-row case is reachable rather than impossible.",
docs/superpowers/plans/refactor-565-complexity-bundle-intake.json:27:    "Terminal-write contract: every contact_csv_uploads terminal write carries the status='pending' predicate. Because only lock-holders change status, the predicate cannot change the outcome for a row that still exists; a 0-row result means the row is GONE (offboarding purge race), which completes the job silently today and MUST continue to.",
docs/superpowers/plans/refactor-565-complexity-bundle-intake.json:28:    "Lock-order contract: in prepareBatch the accounts row lock is taken BEFORE the agent_runs row lock. evaluateBatchGate must therefore be called before the activeParent SELECT ... FOR UPDATE."
docs/superpowers/plans/refactor-565-complexity-bundle-intake.json:31:    "Ingest path terminal write matching 0 rows: REACHABLE, not impossible — the offboarding purge (purge-stages.ts:256) can delete the row between the pending read at ingest.ts:136 and the write at ingest.ts:155/167. Today the unguarded UPDATE matches 0 rows and the job completes normally; the refactor must preserve exactly that. Do NOT assert or throw here.",
docs/superpowers/plans/refactor-565-complexity-bundle-intake.json:32:    "failed-hook and terminalizeUploadForInactiveSubscription terminal write matching 0 rows: legitimate no-op (lost race against a concurrent terminal write / completed job / purge) — must stay silent.",
docs/superpowers/plans/refactor-565-complexity-bundle-intake.json:33:    "prepareBatch and constructBatch re-check the same gate (flag / subscription / offboarding) at two different times by design; sharing the check must NOT collapse them into one evaluation — construction's re-check is the load-bearing one.",
docs/superpowers/plans/refactor-565-complexity-bundle-intake.json:35:    "Calling evaluateBatchGate AFTER prepareBatch's activeParent SELECT ... FOR UPDATE would reverse the accounts->agent_runs lock order on a refactor-only branch. It must be called before.",
