docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-03-645-manual-suppression-paths.md:22:| P-2 | The correction record carries **no FK anywhere**, and **no `account_id` column at all** | Two independent reasons. (a) The suppression row is gone by the time the record is written — that is the point — so an FK to it is impossible, and an FK to `accounts` would let a purge CASCADE away a compliance record. (b) Copying the deleted row's `account_id` in would create a NEW indefinite retention obligation for provenance whose owning row no longer exists, and would make this table "account-linked" to `accountLinkedTablesFromMigrations()` in `src/lib/account-offboarding/__tests__/table-disposition.test.ts` — which fails CI unless the table also joins `TENANT_TABLES`, `TABLE_DISPOSITIONS` and purge verification. The record says WHICH opt-out, WHO removed it and WHY; whose send originally produced it is not part of that sentence |
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-03-645-manual-suppression-paths.md:199:-- src/lib/account-offboarding/__tests__/table-disposition.test.ts — which then
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-03-645-manual-suppression-paths.md:200:-- requires entries in TENANT_TABLES, TABLE_DISPOSITIONS and purge verification
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-03-645-manual-suppression-paths.md:215:-- when not. Nothing in the ledger, the batch build or the offboarding purge
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-03-645-manual-suppression-paths.md:258:| `solicitation_suppression_corrections` | **No TTL.** The record proves an opt-out was removed and by whom; deleting it would erase the only evidence that the removal was audited. Retains `normalized_handle` indefinitely — the minimum needed to identify WHICH opt-out was removed, since `suppression_id` points at a deleted row — matching the retention posture of the `scope='global'` ledger rows it describes (spec D7). It carries **no** `account_id` (plan P-2), so it is not account-linked and correctly absent from `TABLE_DISPOSITIONS` | No poller touches it; the offboarding purge deliberately does not list it, and `table-disposition.test.ts` confirms that is correct rather than an omission because the table has no account-linked column |
