docs/superpowers/plans/feat-695-import-consent-block-reason-intake.json:5:  "goal": "Record the rejection of job_outbox-boundary enforcement for Import consent as ADR 0016, and make guardImportConsent's refusals separable by SQL — for the 7-day job_outbox archival window — by completing the refused outbox row with completion_reason = 'import_consent_blocked'.",
docs/superpowers/plans/feat-695-import-consent-block-reason-intake.json:9:    "No per-state reason values — one 'import_consent_blocked' member; the specific refusal state (pending | declined | expired | missing) stays in the existing structured log line.",
docs/superpowers/plans/feat-695-import-consent-block-reason-intake.json:10:    "No HealthAlertPoller check, no Sentry capture, no PostHog event — a refusal is the guard working, not an incident.",
docs/superpowers/plans/feat-695-import-consent-block-reason-intake.json:19:    "Operator-visible only: a zernio_initial_backfill outbox row refused by guardImportConsent now carries job_outbox.completion_reason = 'import_consent_blocked' instead of NULL, so a policy refusal is separable by SQL from a genuine completed import."
docs/superpowers/plans/feat-695-import-consent-block-reason-intake.json:31:    "Missing businesses row (reason 'missing'): still marked import_consent_blocked — a hand-inserted row for a deleted location is a refusal, not a separate class. Note this is also the case where the refusal state is NOT recoverable from the businesses row, so the log line is the only per-state record.",
docs/superpowers/plans/feat-695-import-consent-block-reason-intake.json:33:    "A row refused as 'pending' whose business later becomes 'accepted': completion_reason stays 'import_consent_blocked' on the historical row — it records that a refusal happened, not current state, and the state at refusal time is NOT re-derivable from the business row afterwards.",
docs/superpowers/plans/feat-695-import-consent-block-reason-intake.json:35:    "Legacy rows refused BEFORE this change keep completion_reason NULL, so NULL does not universally mean 'genuine import' — the operator query is reliable only for post-deployment refusals, and ADR 0016 must say so.",
docs/superpowers/plans/feat-695-import-consent-block-reason-intake.json:87:    "Operational-window signal (new), NOT an audit record: SELECT completion_reason, count(*) FROM job_outbox WHERE topic = 'zernio_initial_backfill' AND status = 'completed' GROUP BY 1 — an 'import_consent_blocked' bucket counts refusals. Trustworthy in exactly one band: rows created after deploy AND completed within the last 7 days. Two independent limits — (a) refusals from before this change are also NULL, so NULL means 'genuine import OR pre-deployment refusal'; (b) ArchivalPoller deletes completed job_outbox rows 7 days after completed_at, and a refusal completes rather than fails, so it takes the 7-day arm. Same life owner_unreachable has always had (ADR 0010) — a property of the sink, not of this ticket. The record that outlives the window is businesses.import_decision / import_decision_at.",
docs/superpowers/plans/feat-695-import-consent-block-reason-intake.json:89:    "How I would know it broke — marker regression: a refusal that leaves completion_reason NULL (the pre-change behaviour) means the guard stopped stamping.",
