docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-f1-owner-unreachable-escalation.md:483:- **Durability ⨯ archival (codex R3-A — OWNER-DECIDED: accept + document):** `ArchivalPoller.ts:42` deletes `completed` job_outbox rows older than 7 days, so an `owner_unreachable` marker is pruned at 7 days. The signal stays durable because the retry arm re-creates a fresh marker every ~2–6h (latest-by-`created_at` is always <7 days while retries run). The only way the signal is lost is if the retry itself STALLS (a `send_notification` stuck `pending`/`dispatching` for >7 days) — which is independently caught by `checkStaleDispatching` / `checkOldestPendingOutbox`. So durability is real but *coupled to the retry loop*; documented here and in ADR 0010. Rejected alternative (excludes `owner_unreachable` markers from `ArchivalPoller` — decouples durability but adds `ArchivalPoller` to the edit surface + complicates retention) — not taken, per LOCKED-minimal scope.
