docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-26-qr-review-request.md:716:- **Description:** One successful **QR redirect** (CONTEXT.md): a customer scanned a location's **Review QR** and was 302-redirected to that location's Google write-review page. Counted AFTER the resolve gates pass (existence, not archived, `subscriptionAllowsQrRedirect`, canonical place id) and never on a refusal — an unavailable-page serve emits nothing (it is a log line, not a metric). v1 counts every successful resolve, HEAD requests and prefetchers included (accepted noise, intake edge case). The name is registered in the `analytics_events.event_name` CHECK by **migration 115** — the DB CHECK, not the TS allowlist, is what admits the name.
