docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-07-ws3-guardian-escalation.md:1432:Query: `SELECT e.id, e.status, e.business_id AS esc_business_id, e.account_id, e.review_id, e.triage_severity, e.triage_source, e.triage_suggested_action, e.triage_issues, r.reviewer_name, r.star_rating, r.review_text FROM review_escalations e JOIN reviews r ON r.id = e.review_id WHERE e.id = ${input.escalationId}`. Guards, in order: not found → `fail('escalation_not_found')`; `esc_business_id !== input.businessId` → `fail('business_id_mismatch')`; `status === ESCALATION_STATUS.RESOLVED` → `skip('already_resolved')` (acknowledged still sends — the notice may be what acknowledges it elsewhere; only resolved is moot). Business query: copy the auto-post-notice business query verbatim (it already selects name/display_label/subscription/offboarding projection; `google_maps_url` may be dropped). Same archived/offboarding skips.
