    92	## Two limits, stated rather than papered over
    93	
    94	### The highest-volume refusal cannot be explained
    95	
    96	`AutoApprovalBlockReason` — 22 members at
    97	`worker/jobs/response-generation/auto-approval.ts:37` — is the per-review answer
    98	to "we drafted a reply and did not auto-post it, why". It reaches only a
    99	`logger.log` call at `persist.ts:570-576`. The `policy_gate` run-spine step
   100	records `decision: 'held_for_owner'` with no reason.
   101	
   102	**So the Refusal Log reports THAT a draft was held for the owner, never WHY.**
   103	
   104	This partially falsifies the premise the feature was scoped on — "RepWorth does
   105	not discard refusal reasons". It holds for the seven sources shipped. It does
   106	not hold for this one, which is probably the most common refusal in the system.
   107	
   108	Closing it needs a capture change: either a `block_reasons` key on the existing
   109	`policy_gate` step detail (no migration — `agent_run_steps.detail` is JSONB and
   110	`step_key` has no CHECK), or a column. Both were deliberately out of scope; the
   111	owner chose to ship the available sources and record the gap. Whoever closes it
   112	should know it only fills forward from deploy.
   113	
   114	### One timestamp can still drift
   115	
   116	`solicitation_outreach` has no disposition timestamp, and its withheld arm has
   117	**two writers** with two different correct answers:
   118	
   119	| Reason | Writer | Anchor |
   120	|---|---|---|
   121	| `moderation_high`, `render_failed`, `lint_failed` | `ask-generation.ts` inserts the row already withheld | `rendered_at` — `NOT NULL`, never updated |
   122	| the other five | `dispatch.ts` `commitWithhold`, which sets `agent_run_id` atomically | `COALESCE(agent_runs.started_at, updated_at)` |
   123	
   124	The partition is exactly `RenderWithholdReason`
   125	(`src/lib/solicitation/outreach.ts:525`), so the split is the shape of the data
   126	rather than a special case. Neither anchor is correct alone: `rendered_at`
   127	predates the dispatch half, and `run.started_at` is the batch parent's start for
   128	the render half.
   129	
   130	`updated_at` is a general mutation timestamp a later write can move. It survives
   131	only as the fallback for a dispatch-time withhold whose best-effort lazy-child
   132	attach left `agent_run_id` NULL. **Such a row can still drift between windows.**
   133	Closing that needs a column, which this ADR's no-migration decision excludes.
   134	
   135	## Consequences
   136	
   137	- The owner gets a durable record of restraint. A competitor copies a feature in
   138	  a weekend; a two-year record of principled refusals is a time series, not a
   139	  function.
   140	- The two admin-only tables stay admin-only. Widening either is a separate
   141	  decision requiring its own ADR.
   142	- The log **under-reports the reply lane** until the capture gap above is
   143	  closed. Any claim made from its counts must be read with that in mind.
   144	- Adding a member to `WithholdReason`, `AutoPolicyDowngradeReason`,
   145	  `AutonomySuspensionTrigger` or `RenderWithholdReason` breaks the build until

